! DF on a REFILL ADDRESS -- Reference Manual p.32, class 3, the half of
! it that names operations: "the refill address used in index refill
! operations and the operations REFILL and REFILL ON COUNT ZERO."
!
!
! SUPERSEDED 2026-09-24, AND THE CORRECTION MATTERS MORE THAN THE
! PROGRAM.  The "weaker standard" note above rests on the claim that no
! listing here tests DF.  THAT CLAIM IS FALSE.  jb_ax5b routine 1260
! TEST 8C -- PDF pp.76-83, octal 022546.00-022732.40, labels
! I60127-I60146 -- is a dedicated test of the DF AND IF INDICATORS
! under four enable/mask conditions, verified first-hand at 400 dpi:
!
!   I60127 LVI,$X1,I60AD1  -TEST 8C CHECKS DF + IF UNDER 4 CONDS,
!                          -1. DISABL MASK 0 FETCH OK IND NO INT
!                          -2. DIAABL MASK 1 FETCH OK NO IND NO INT
!                          -3. ENABLE MASK 0 FETCH OK IND ON NO INT
!                          -4. ENABLE MASK 1 NO FETCH IND ON INTRPT
!
! Condition 4 is the MASK-DEPENDENT half these programs scope out.  So
! this file was written to a weaker standard than was available, in a
! document this project had already read, thirty pages before the
! routine whose misreading produced the claim.  The program is not
! thereby wrong -- but it is not the strongest evidence available, and
! TEST 8C is the acceptance test it should be checked against.  See
! docs/NEXT.md item 2.
! WEAKER STANDARD, hand-written from p.32, for the reason
! df_data_fetch_alarm.strap gives at length: no listing this project
! has read tests DF at all.  This is the companion to that program --
! it covers R and RCZ; that one covers p.32's class 1.  The OTHER nine
! refill-read sites, the ones progressive indexing and count-branching
! issue, are still unmonitored and this program does not touch them.
!
! WHERE THE SIGNAL GOES, and the constraint that decides it.  Routine
! 1238's test 2 (jb_ax4b p.58-59) established that a refill address of
! 1-15 is SUPPRESSED and that word 0 does refill -- "CHK REFILL FRM
! LOCN 0" against "CHK NO REFILL FRM LOCNS 1 THROUGH 17" -- which the
! model spells refillLegal.  RCZ adds a second gate: it "acts only if
! its count is zero" (p.26).  A refill that either gate suppresses
! READS NOTHING, and p.32's own first sentence is "all storage
! addresses ACTUALLY USED by the CPU in the course of an operation are
! subject to address monitoring."  So dfSignal sits INSIDE both gates,
! and the block below that runs RCZ with a non-zero count is what makes
! that placement a tested claim rather than a comment.
!
! AND ONLY A REFILL ADDRESS OF 32 OR MORE CAN EVER SIGNAL.  p.31's
! carve-out means words 0 and 4-31 never do; 1-3 always do but are the
! permanently protected registers; 1-15 are suppressed anyway and 16-31
! are the index registers.  So the monitored area here holds ordinary
! core, which is the only place a refill source can be that matters.
!
! MASK-ZERO ONLY, same scope as df_data_fetch_alarm.strap and for the
! same reason: p.32's mask-one behaviour is suppression and
! termination, and this model has no termination mechanism.
!
! Instructions: BD, BE, LVI, SV, LX, SX, KV, R, RCZ, NOP, BB, BB1,
! BBZ, BZB, B, BEW -- all implemented.

        SLC, (8)4100.0
START   BD,  $+.32                   ! disable: words 2 and 3 are protected
        LVI, $X13, TBL
        SV,  $X13, $IA
        LVI, $X13, RFSRC
        SV,  $X13, $LB               ! lower boundary := RFSRC
        LVI, $X13, ABOVE
        SV,  $X13, $UB               ! upper boundary := ABOVE
        BBZ, 3.57, $+1.0             ! control bit := 0: signal INSIDE
        BBZ, 12.20, $+1.0            ! DF's mask bit := 0
        BE,  $+.32
!
! ---- 1. R refilling an INDEX REGISTER from the monitored area -----
        LX,  $X0,  K1                ! K1 is outside; its refill is RFSRC
        R,   $X0
        BZB, $DF,  $                 ! hang if the refill address missed DF
        BB,  $IF,  $                 ! hang if it lit bit 21 instead of 20
        BBZ, $DF,  $+1.0
        KV,  $X0,  RFCOPY            ! and the refill LANDED: mask zero,
        BZB, $XE,  $                 !   so the operation proceeds
!
! ---- 2. RCZ with a NON-ZERO count refills nothing ----------------
!   The gate that makes the placement above a claim.  K2's refill names
!   the same monitored word, and RCZ must not read it.
        LX,  $X1,  K2                ! count non-zero, refill -> RFSRC
        RCZ, $X1
        BB,  $DF,  $                 ! hang if a suppressed refill lit DF
        KV,  $X1,  K2COPY            ! and nothing was refilled
        BZB, $XE,  $
!
! ---- 3. RCZ with a zero count does refill ------------------------
        LX,  $X1,  K1                ! count 0, refill -> RFSRC
        RCZ, $X1
        BZB, $DF,  $                 ! hang if RCZ's refill missed DF
        BBZ, $DF,  $+1.0
!
! ---- 4. R whose operand word is in EXTERNAL MEMORY ---------------
!   Two sequential reads: the index word at the effective address, then
!   the word its refill field names.  EXIDX is OUTSIDE the area, so
!   only the second read can signal.
        LX,  $X2,  K1
        SX,  $X2,  EXIDX
        R,   EXIDX
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, $DF,  $                 ! hang if the external path missed DF
        BBZ, $DF,  $+1.0
!
! ---- 5. and that path's own operand read is a STORE --------------
!   EXIN sits INSIDE the area and R writes it back, so p.32 puts its
!   read on the DS side.  Its refill names a word OUTSIDE, so DF has
!   nothing else to fire on and a model that signalled DF for `rw`
!   would be caught here.  The NOPs give the interruption its quiescent
!   boundary -- see df_data_fetch_alarm.strap's note.
        R,   EXIN
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BB,  $DF,  $                 ! hang if the operand read lit DF
        BZB, 6.0,  $                 ! hang if DS's routine did not run
        BBZ, 6.0,  $+1.0
        B,   PASS
PASS    BEW, $
!
! ---- constants, all OUTSIDE the monitored area -------------------
        SLC, (8)4200.0
K1      XW, 0, 0, RFSRC              ! count 0, refill -> RFSRC (inside)
K2      XW, 0, 7, RFSRC              ! count 7: RCZ must not fire
K2COPY  XW, 0, 7, RFSRC              ! ... and $X1 must still equal it
RFCOPY  XW, (8)123456.76, (8)543210, (8)123456
EXIDX   NOP                          ! scratch: an index word is stored here
        NOP
OUTSRC  XW, (8)765432.10, 0, 0       ! a refill source OUTSIDE the area
!
! ---- the monitored area ------------------------------------------
        SLC, (8)4300.0
RFSRC   XW, (8)123456.76, (8)543210, (8)123456   ! == the lower boundary
EXIN    XW, 0, 0, OUTSRC             ! an index word INSIDE the area
ABOVE   DD(BU,64,8), 0               ! == the upper boundary, first word out
!
! ---- the interruption table --------------------------------------
        SLC, (8)4500.0
TBL     DD, 0
        SLC, (8)4523.0
DSRTN   BB1, 6.0, $+1.0              ! entry 19 = DS
        END, START
